      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we first list out the first six prime numbers:\n\n1. \\( p_1 = 2 \\)\n2. \\( p_2 = 3 \\)\n3. \\( p_3 = 5 \\)\n4. \\( p_4 = 7 \\)\n5. \\( p_5 = 11 \\)\n6. \\( p_6 = 13 \\)\n\nNext, we find the sum of the first five primes:\n\n\\[\n2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11 = 28\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 28 is divided by the sixth prime, which is 13:\n\n\\[\n28 \\div 13\n\\]\n\nTo do this, we perform the division:\n\n\\[\n28 \\div 13 \\approx 2.1538\n\\]\n\nTo find the remainder, we multiply the quotient by the divisor and subtract this from 28:\n\n\\[\n28 - (2 \\times 13) = 28 - 26 = 2\n\\]\n\nSo, the remainder when 28 is divided by 13 is 2.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
